#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:22
#: 7f1170b17caa4a819c95a7a206f91e4b
msgid "Flightgear screenshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:25
#: 3877f19a349d4c3e98fc4efd35f4ba1b
msgid "Things you need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:27
#: 271232585a344b559149d8f6908e57ec
msgid "`Flightgear <http://www.flightgear.org/>`__ (tested Flight Gear v2.x, currently at v3.4)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:29
#: f18683ee66a249debd625dc1d7f796ab
msgid "`Mission Planner <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Tools/MissionPlanner/MissionPlanner-latest.msi>`__ (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:31
#: 676b268146474baca54ee99b84ec152b
msgid "ArduPilot HIL on your APM (via APM Planner, currently (April 2013) only v2.68 HIL works, see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:33
#: 31daa4af75794174b43d8702f164c647
msgid "`Mavlink.xml <https://github.com/dronekit/ardupilot-releases/blob/master/Tools/FlightGear/MAVLink.xml>`__ data format file for flightgear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:35
#: 321799b102084f2294f5eb98736365c1
msgid "Recommended for Windows OS: the file: \\ `system.fgfsrc <https://code.google.com/p/ardupilot-mega/downloads/detail?name=system.fgfsrc>`__ placed into the \"C:\\\\Program Files (x86)\\\\FlightGear\\\\data\" folder. This will load the Rascal RC plane and a few other parameters. More information on what is loaded \\ `here <http://wiki.flightgear.org/Fgfsrc>`__, you can alter it to your own requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:44
#: 5a94acff99244f13bc0e19596e7eadf0
msgid "How to make it work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:48
#: 45e2991f82654d6eba0c406d452234cb
msgid "Safety first: Disconnect the 3 wires from your brushless motor otherwise it will start when you advance the throttle (if in manual mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:52
#: 991d3f55542042a99763954584f14129
msgid "Download and install the FlightGear Flight Sim if you have not already"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:54
#: 0af65d9c8b3a4c0a8382cdf034abf18d
msgid "Copy Mavlink.xml to C:\\\\Program Files (x86)\\\\FlightGear\\\\data\\\\Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:56
#: 6c3dadcd079a4ab6814dadfd48751b2a
msgid "In the Mission Planner > 'Configuration tab \\| Adv Parameter List' save your current parameters so you can reload them after the simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:59
#: 7d3412f5380c4597828fcca8c55d8909
msgid "In the Firmware tab of the MP, choose 'Pick previous firmware', from the drop down list pick the 4th one down, firmware should show as Plane v2.68, then click 'HIL Simulator \\| Plane' to load the Plane firmware onto your APM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:63
#: 5ac65e72703649ce93df7bd30aa53790
msgid "Connect to the APM, then open the Simulation tab of the Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:65
#: 1d47aa21b7f04e7aafc6555a417bccb3
msgid "Check the FlightGear radio button, then click the 'Start FG Plane' button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:67
#: 11a94bb7f76847d5b759cfbaf885e20e
msgid "After FG has finished loading click the 'Sim Link Start/Stop' button in the MP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:69
#: d4cdf1f5409e41c293a192397ee080a0
msgid "In FG press ' v ' on the keyboard to get an outside view of the plane, ' x ' to zoom, move your aileron stick to see if the planes ailerons move, great if they do, go through this list again if not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:72
#: 76975e9efec048a892b7f795e5e86dd4
msgid "Now in the Mission Planner do your usual radio setup including calibration and mode switch setup, then you can fly Missions and test the APM just like you would on a real plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/flightgear-hardware-in-the-loop-simulation.rst:78
#: e260256b67cd4e90a419b8d3b051db3f
msgid "If you used the file \"`system.fgfsrc <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/advanced_user_tools/windows_parameter_file_for_flightgear_HIL_simulator_system.fgfsrc.zip>`__\\ \" then you can just increase your throttle to fly the Rascal plane. If you didn't and are flying the default Cessna, hold down 's' on the keyboard to start the plane's engine, then advance your throttle to take off."
msgstr ""
